</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:129%;">Performance and Speedup Comparison on LLaDA Between 5-Shot and 8-Shot Settings at Generation Length 1024.<span id="S4.T4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
This table compares the accuracy and throughput speedups of different decoding strategies under 5-shot and 8-shot configurations using a generation length of 1024. The results demonstrate how increased prefill length enhances the effectiveness of caching strategies, particularly for DualCache.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
